# {{.Name}}

A [Hydrogen](https://github.com/hydrogencms/hydrogen) project.

```sh
hydrogen dev            # serve on :8080 with live reload (SQLite in .work/, no setup)
hydrogen config:check   # validate configuration and schema
```

On the first start `hydrogen dev` prints a link that creates the first administrator in the admin. Content types live
in `schema/` (`article.yaml` is an example); `hydrogen dev` regenerates the typed code in `gen/` when they change.

Admin extensions live in `admin/` (Svelte custom elements on `@hydrogencms/admin-sdk`; Node is only needed
here, not for the Go server). `cd admin && npm install && npm run build` writes `admin/dist/elements.js`; then
uncomment the `admin:` block in `config/app.yaml` to load it. The example `x-hello` is a field widget: give a
string field `admin: { widget: hello }` in the schema. For hot reload, run `npm run dev` in `admin/` and start
`ADMIN_ELEMENTS_DEV_URL=http://localhost:5174 hydrogen dev` (Vite's `base` in `vite.config.ts` must be
`<admin.prefix>/x/dev/`). The CSP allows inline styles but no scripts. `npm run dev` assumes the admin prefix `/admin`; set `ADMIN_PREFIX`
if you changed `admin.prefix`.
{{if .Core}}
`@hydrogencms/admin-sdk` is installed from your hydrogen checkout (`file:` dependency in `admin/package.json`).
{{end}}

Configuration lives in `config/`; set `DATABASE_URL` to use Postgres.
